abstract: "The Roman Notebooks are a colenction of Jupyter Notebook tutorials and Science Workflows focused
on the Roman Wide Field Instrument (WFI) for  observation planning, image simulation with Roman-I-Sim, 
calibration with RomanCal, and scientific analysis of WFI data products including photometry, galaxy shapes,
and grism spectroscopy. The notebooks are primarily designed for the Roman Research Nexus cloud platform but 
include instructions for local execution. They serve as practical guides to prepare the community for Roman
science and are intended to be cited in publications that make use of these resources."
repository-code: "https://github.com/spacetelescope/roman_notebooks"
